.TH ASCIIFY 1 "October 2026" "asciify 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asciify \- convert images to ASCII art or colored block art in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asciify
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIIMAGE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asciify
draws an image in the terminal. In
.B ascii
mode each character cell shows one pixel, picked from a ramp of characters by
brightness and, in color, drawn in the pixel's own 24-bit color. In
.B blocks
mode each cell is an upper half block whose foreground and background colors
show two pixels, which doubles the vertical detail.
.PP
.I IMAGE
is a file in any format Pillow reads (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, TIFF and
more), an http or https URL, or
.B \-
to read the image from standard input.
.PP
On a terminal the output fits the window unless
.B \-\-width
is given. Transparent pixels are left blank.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Output width in characters. Default: fit the terminal, or 100 when the output
is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fBascii\fR|\fBblocks\fR
Characters by brightness (the default), or half-block cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fBauto\fR|\fBalways\fR|\fBnever\fR
.B auto
(the default) colors output to a terminal unless the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable is set, colors HTML files, and writes plain text
otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-nc ", " \-\-no\-color
Same as
.BR "\-\-color never" .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-invert
Invert brightness, for terminals with a light background.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-chars " " \fIRAMP\fR
Characters for ascii mode, ordered from least to most ink, for example
\(aq .:\-=+*#%@\(aq. At least two characters.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Save to
.I FILE
instead of printing. A name ending in
.B .html
or
.B .htm
saves a web page; anything else saves text (with color escapes only with
.BR "\-\-color always" ).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-animate
Play an animated GIF or WebP in the terminal. Ctrl+C stops it.
.TP
.BR \-\-loop " " \fIN\fR
With
.BR \-\-animate ,
play
.I N
times. 0, the default, loops until stopped.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
asciify photo.jpg
asciify \-m blocks photo.jpg
asciify \-w 80 \-\-invert logo.png
asciify \-a \-\-loop 3 dance.gif
asciify https://example.com/cat.png \-o cat.html
curl \-s https://example.com/cat.png | asciify \-
.RE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value,
.B \-\-color auto
does not color terminal output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the image can't be read or the output can't be written,
2 for invalid options.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Mark Mysler.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/markmysler/asciify
